Here's what changed in fault_reload.c and why it's correct:

The MCE decode chain (mce_register_decode_chain, struct mce, MCI_STATUS_*) is wrapped in #ifdef CONFIG_X86. In its place, an ARM64 die_notifier block under #elif defined(CONFIG_ARM64) registers fr_arm64_die_handler which fires on ARM_DIE_SERROR — the ARM64 equivalent of a machine check. It increments the same g_mce_uc_events counter so the procfs stats remain meaningful on both arches.

The entire RAPL block (rapl_read_energy, rapl_init_unit, rapl_poll_worker, all MSR globals) is wrapped in #ifdef CONFIG_X86. In the ARM64 init path enable_rapl is forced to false immediately, so the RAPL delayed work is never scheduled and the RAPL cancel in exit is never reached. The hwmon voltage polling path — which is the detection method that actually works on the IPQ807x — is completely untouched and runs identically on both arches.
